From c22247432263d384d01a4639f6165a5f1a39f3b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SIGF <noreply@sigf.ai>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:24:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Load libsm64 at runtime from sm64.dll instead of compiling it
 into er_mario.dll

er_mario.dll no longer contains libsm64 (SM64's decompiled code and Mario's
mesh from the SM64 decompilation). src/sm64.rs keeps the same 30 functions
with the same names and signatures; each now calls the function of that name
in sm64.dll, loaded once with LoadLibraryW from the mod folder (next to
er_mario.dll) and resolved with GetProcAddress. build.rs, which compiled
libsm64 into the mod, is removed; sm64.dll is built from the libsm64 folder
with its own Makefile (make lib). Without sm64.dll the mod logs why and shows
a banner instead of starting Mario.

MIT, like the mod.
